   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Shrink Burst Text\n\nA word squeezes tight and trembles, then bursts into letters that fly outward, spin and fade; the word slides back up into place and the cycle repeats.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 7.4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A word or message should be built up, shaken and blown apart as an impact beat.\n- A looping 'send' or 'boom' moment on a short phrase.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text must stay readable throughout: it is fully gone for about a second each cycle.\n- Long sentences.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Hello there\"\n- font_size (number, 12-300): Font size, default 110\n- spread (number, 0.2-2): Spread, default 1\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/codse/animata. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
